  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher volumes of advanced chips crossing borders increase alternative sourcing and inventory buffers for European manufacturers, directly reducing reliance on single suppliers and chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">euro_security_autonomy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::adv_chip_flow_rate" target="global_financial_stress::project_financing_cost" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">An increased, reliable cross‑border flow of advanced chips reduces supply‑chain and delivery risk for AI projects and lowers required upfront capex and contingency, which directly reduces lenders' and equity providers' required returns.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::adv_chip_flow_rate" target="iran_regional_escalation::tanker_positioning_rate" id="0">
