<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_balance" target="euro_security_autonomy::industrial_investment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A shift in the military balance toward a greater Russian capability raises European threat perceptions and defense procurement commitments, prompting increased private and public capital expenditures into domestic defense and heavy industry capacity.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">euro_security_autonomy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_balance" target="global_financial_stress::project_financing_cost" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">A shift in military balance that increases the likelihood of a prolonged or regionally expanded conflict raises sovereign and supply‑risk premia for long‑dated infrastructure and tech projects, leading lenders to charge higher spreads and push up blended financing costs.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_balance" target="iran_regional_escalation::crude_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An improvement in Russia's military balance (greater ability to secure export infrastructure and maintain output) reduces physical disruption risk and market risk premia for Russian supplies, lowering benchmark crude prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::military_balance" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::congressional_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A deterioration in the battlefield balance (adversary gains) heightens perceived strategic vulnerability among lawmakers, triggering more frequent hearings and oversight focused on technology transfers and corporate links to geopolitical competitors.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
