<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::sanction_pressure_level" target="euro_security_autonomy::policy_adjustment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in sanction pressure on regional actors forces European governments and the EU to rapidly alter regulations and deploy emergency fiscal/subsidy measures (e.g., energy relief, exemptions, blocking statutes) to protect firms and maintain trade, increasing the rate of policy adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">euro_security_autonomy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::sanction_pressure_level" target="global_financial_stress::market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating sanctions force banks and trading houses to limit counterparty exposure and withdraw from sanctioned corridors, reducing intermediation and depth in energy, credit and FX markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::sanction_pressure_level" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::congressional_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A rapid increase in sanctions and enforcement actions tied to an Iran escalation prompts congressional committees to open hearings and oversight into export-control compliance and corporate conduct related to tech transfers, raising the frequency and intensity of scrutiny.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::sanction_pressure_level" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::reexport_leakage_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter and broader sanctions incentivize traders and intermediaries to route controlled or sensitive hardware through secondary markets and opaque intermediaries to evade restrictions, increasing the probability of re‑export leakage to restricted end destinations.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
