<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::crude_price_level" target="euro_security_autonomy::industrial_investment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained increases in crude prices raise operating and input costs for energy‑intensive sectors, prompting firms to delay, cancel or downscale new capital projects and shift CAPEX toward energy efficiency rather than expansion, reducing industrial investment flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_regional_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">euro_security_autonomy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_escalation::crude_price_level" target="global_financial_stress::policy_rate_expectation" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained jump in benchmark crude raises near‑term headline inflation and inflation expectations, causing markets to price in faster or larger central‑bank tightening.</data>
