  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising expected policy rates strengthen the US dollar and increase carry/hedging costs for non‑USD buyers, reducing near‑term import demand and exerting downward pressure on benchmark crude prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_financial_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_escalation</data>
