  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher expected policy rates raise domestic borrowing costs and fiscal pressures in sanctioning states, reducing political appetite and budgetary room to sustain or escalate costly sanctions packages.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_financial_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
